{
    "background_story": "Navy was a sturdy tugboat with a distinctive bullnose bow, designed for navigating the rough waters of the North Sea. Built in the 1950s, she had a reputation for being one of the most reliable and hardworking vessels in the fleet. Navy's bullnose design allowed her to push and pull massive cargo ships with ease, earning her the respect of her human crew. Despite being decommissioned in the 1980s, Navy was restored to her former glory by a team of dedicated enthusiasts. Today, she can be found chugging along the coast, her bullnose bow proudly leading the way, a testament to the ingenuity of her designers and the dedication of those who kept her afloat.",
